    "narrative": "Today\u2019s optimal build for Ghost Ride the WHIP leans heavily on favorable matchups against vulnerable arms like Sugano and Buehler. The premier play of the day is **Corbin Carroll** (87.14), who sits just shy of elite status. His projection is bolstered by a high-upside matchup against Sugano and a significant stolen base probability boost stemming from the pitcher's slow delivery, a key factor given our league's weighting. **Tyler Soderstrom** (73.03) and **Seiya Suzuki** (69.20) are our next most reliable anchors; both benefit from strong platoon advantages and favorable SP_xERA marks, making them high-floor starters in our 5x5 pursuit. **James Wood** also earns a prime spot with a 67.31 score, as his elite xwOBA profile and high-leadoff position against Elder provide the perfect engine for our Run production.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Brice Turang**, who finished just outside the starting cut with a 50.85 score. While **Brice Turang** possesses the elite sprint speed we covet, he is neutralized by a difficult matchup against Wrobleski and the inherent park factors working against him today. Consequently, he loses out to the higher projected offensive ceilings of **Zach McKinstry** (62.14) and **Mickey Moniak** (65.50), whose platoon advantages against Akin and Soroka, respectively, drive their efficiency scores significantly higher. We are also monitoring the lineup status of **Gabriel Moreno** and **Mickey Moniak**; should they shift lower in the batting order than our projections anticipate, their scores will regress, though their current profiles remain high enough to justify the risk. While **Vinnie Pasquantino** (55.60) faces a tougher test against the efficient Gilbert, his strong platoon edge ensures he remains in our UTIL slot over speculative bench pieces like **Kyle Karros** or **Dalton Rushing**.",
